note RFC 6298 2.2 to 2.5 with nonzero samples (review finding 5). The first sample R
note sets SRTT = R and RTTVAR = R/2 (kept as 8 SRTT in kSRT and 4 RTTVAR in kRVR); each
note later one RTTVAR = 3/4 RTTVAR + 1/4 |SRTT - R| (both signs of the difference) and
note SRTT = 7/8 SRTT + 1/8 R; RTO = SRTT + 4 RTTVAR. Karn: an ACK below the end of the
note timed segment takes no sample, and one timed segment gives one sample. A sample
note over 60 s counts as 60 s, and the RTO is at most 60 s (2.5). The payload of every
note segment sent is checked against the stream written.
