note The send ring past 65536 octets: 100,000 bytes go out on one connection with the
note payload of every segment checked against the stream written; the receive ring
note likewise, 70,000 bytes read back. tread returns at most what is stored and at most
note what was asked. A window update waits for one own MSS of new space (receiver silly
note window avoidance, RFC 9293 3.8.6.2.2). Data written in syn-received goes out from
note stream offset 0 once the handshake ACK arrives. The receive buffer takes 65535
note bytes, and the ACK then offers a zero window.
