note RFC 9293 3.10.7.4 and RFC 5961 5: in syn-received an ACK at or below ISS or above
note SND.NXT gets a RST at that ACK and changes nothing; in ESTABLISHED an ACK above
note SND.MAX or below SND.UNA - 65535 is answered with an ACK and dropped, while
note SND.UNA - 65535 itself is taken as old. A retransmitted SYN or SYN-ACK carries only
note the MSS option, and its timer is armed again at the doubled RTO. The send window
note comes from a segment with SND.UNA =< SEG.ACK and a newer SEG.SEQ (or the same with
note SEG.ACK >= SND.WL2), not from a retransmitted older segment nor an old ACK; a
note zero-window ACK restarts the retry count. The bad syn-received ACK leaves the window.
