note RFC 9293 3.8.6.1 and RFC 1122 4.2.2.17, zero windows. A FIN outstanding when the
note window closes: the timeout resends the FIN alone (it probes; no data octet goes
note past the stream), and the FIN goes again when the window opens.
note An idle block sent a zero window arms no persist timer; one unsent octet arms it
note one RTO out, and the probe carries that octet at SND.UNA with no RTT sample; an
note acknowledged probe with the window still closed waits one RTO for the next; an
note opened window disarms it, so a later close starts afresh. A probe from a timeout
note with data in flight leaves SND.MAX.
